    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to introduce a fine red brick period residence. Rich in period features including high ceilings, wonderful fireplaces, coving and centre Rose. No. 20 would be an ideal family home in a superb location.\nThe interior is bright and spacious throughout with rooms of elegant proportions being enhanced by original period detail. Accommodation comprises 90sq.m with smart entrance hallway, two grand reception rooms and extended kitchen while upstairs there are two double bedrooms and main bathroom.\nThis is a most desirable location within the ever-popular Stoneybatter Village, walking distance to all amenities, including the new Technological University Dublin at Grangegorman, Smithfield Village, Phibsboro and excellent transport links; the Luas green line which is only a 12 minute walk from the house and great city bus links. The North Circular Road is an airy wide Avenue with mature trees and a short stroll from the gates of the Phoenix Park/Chesterfield Avenue and Heuston train station. There are local shopping facilities and trendy cafes on Manor Street and the Zoological gardens, Farmleigh Estate and Ashtown Castle are also close by. Some of the best schools on Dublin's northside are within easy access including St. Declan's CBS, Belvedere and Mount Carmel. Dublin Airport is a 10-minute drive away, while the M50 sits just 2km north of the area.\nViewing is very highly recommended"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 8.3m x 1.5m\nLarge entrance hallway with original ceiling coving and centre rose, fitted carpets and wooden wall cladding - original staircase\n\nReception Room 1 - 4m x 3.85m\nBright and spacious front reception room with fitted carpets, tiled fireplace and high ceilings.\n\nReception Room 2 - \nSecond reception room with high ceilings, carpets and tiled open fireplace\n\nKitchen - 3.2m x 2.1m\nExtended kitchen with traditional fitted presses and vinyl floors - access to rear garden\n\nStairs and landing - 4m x 1.6m\nWith fitted carpets\n\nBathroom - 3.4m x 2.1m\nLarge bathroom on the return with vinyl floors, bath wc and whb, mid century wall tiling - access to hot press\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.2m x 3.9m\nMain double bedroom to front with fitted carpets, original fireplace and high ceilings\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.1m x 3.7m\nRear double with original open fireplace and fitted carpets\n\nOutside rear - \nRear walled garden stocked with Fuchsia, Palm, Ivy and Jasmine\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Centrally located Red brick period property</li><li> Spacious accommodation throughout</li><li> c. 1890</li><li> Two large reception rooms</li><li> Large bathroom on return</li><li> Situated between Blackhorse Avenue and Marlborough Road</li><li> 300m from the Phoenix Park, 700m to TUD Grangegorman</li><li> 20 minute walk to Hueston Station, 12 minutes to LUAS</li><li> Adjacent proposed DART station</li><li> 3.1km to GPO Dublin City Centre</li><li> Easy access to M50 intersection and Dublin Airport</ul>"
      },
